  "title": "A Complete Hamiltonicity Atlas for Acyclic-Orientation Flip Graphs Through Six Vertices",
  "batch_label": "50",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Under the two-item cyclic-Gray-code convention fixed in problem.md, for every connected unlabeled loopless simple graph G with 2 <= |V(G)| <= 6, AO(G) has a Hamiltonian cycle if and only if sigma(G)=0. The complete domain has 142 isomorphism classes by orders 2,3,4,5,6 in counts 1,2,6,21,112. Exactly 125 classes are Hamiltonian, in counts 1,2,5,18,99 by order; they are exactly the sigma-zero entries of evidence/atlas-through-6.json and each has the explicit cycle in evidence/hamilton-cycles.json. The other 17 classes are non-Hamiltonian by parity imbalance, with canonical graph6 identifiers C], DFw, DLs, D]{, E?~o, E@vg, E@vo, EBj?, EBjW, EBjg, EBz_, EBzw, EB~o, EJeg, EJnW, ELvg, E]~o. Consequently sigma(G)=0 is sufficient throughout the frozen domain and there are no counterexamples, minimum-order or otherwise, in it.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
